From: Igor Velkov <325961+iav@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:50:00 +0000
Subject: rtc: pcf8563: pass the driver data to the alarm interrupt handler

pcf8563_irq() takes its dev_id as struct pcf8563, but probe still
registers the interrupt with the i2c client. The first alarm then
reads through a bogus regmap pointer and oopses, the level-low INT
is never acknowledged, and the interrupt gets disabled as spurious.

Only an RTC that has an interrupt (client->irq > 0) reaches this path.

Tested on ODROID-HC4 with the INT line wired to GPIOX_5 by an overlay:
the alarm interrupt fires once, the alarm flag is cleared, no oops.

Fixes: 00f1bb9b8486 ("rtc: pcf8563: Switch to regmap")
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pcf8563.c
@@ -529,7 +529,7 @@
 		err = devm_request_threaded_irq(&client->dev, client->irq,
 				NULL, pcf8563_irq,
 				IRQF_SHARED | IRQF_ONESHOT | irqflags,
-				pcf8563_driver.driver.name, client);
+				pcf8563_driver.driver.name, pcf8563);
 		if (err) {
 			dev_err(&client->dev, "unable to request IRQ %d\n",
 								client->irq);
